# PROVENANCE: measured from a factory-fresh genuine DESFire EV3 2K with Proxmark3 on 2026-11-01
# (random UID; PICC master key at its all-zero default). Same card and batch as
# hardware_physical_ev3_2k_value_rights.vec.
# PROVISIONAL BATCH "value-rights-2026-11-01": carries `capture-batch: value-rights-2026-11-01` and
# `capture-status: provisional`, so it can be thrown away with the rest of the batch if the card
# proves faulty (see docs/capture-batches.md).
#
# What this measures: how a value file in ENCIPHERED mode (communication mode 03) treats Debit and
# Credit sent plain and sent enciphered, depending on which right authorises the command and which
# key the session holds. The application has two keys at their zero default. Authentication is
# real DES (legacy), the card's random recovered from its first answer and replayed with
# `inject-random`. Enciphered commands use the legacy session key (RndA[0..3]||RndB[0..3], both
# key halves being equal) and "send mode" DES: amount, CRC16, zero padding.
# Observed:
#   * Unauthenticated, a free right makes the command plain and it works plain.
#   * Authenticated, if the session key matches ANY right that can authorise the command, the
#     file's mode applies and the command must be enciphered (the plain form answers 7E).
#   * Authenticated, if the key matches none of them but one of them is free, the command is plain
#     (the enciphered form answers 7E).
#   * So the mode follows the right that actually authorised the command, not the Write right.
name: genuine EV3 2K enciphered value file, Debit and Credit plain versus enciphered by authorising right (provisional batch)
case-id: hardware-physical-ev3-2k-value-comm-modes
origin: physical-card
capture-batch: value-rights-2026-11-01
capture-status: provisional
feature-version: 6
source: physical-card-proxmark3
requires: auth-d40
uid: 04112233445566
picc-generation: EV3
picc-storage: 2048
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-key-len: 16
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-hardware-version: 04010133001605
picc-software-version: 04010103001605

